# Backend conventions

## References

- Simple: `unit.route` → controller → service → mapper → repo
- Scoped: `expense-category.*` (`UserAccessRepo` + `getScopeIdsForUser`)
- Tx: `expense.service` create/edit/remove (`withTransaction`)
- TRY NOT TO copy: `order.service`, `statistic.service`, `site.service`

## Naming

- Files singular: `product.service.ts`, `order-status.route.ts`
- Types often plural: `GetProductsPayload`, `parseGetProductStockStatuses`
- Parsers: `parseCreateX(x) => createXSchema.parse(x)`

Type suffixes: `*Query` (z.input) · `*Payload` (z.output, service input) · `*Response` · `*RepoPayload` / `*RepoResult` · `*DB` · `*DTO` (from `@remnant/shared`)

## Routes

`api/<entity>/<method>` — typically `GET /get`, `POST /create|edit|remove`

Order: `upload?` → validate → `checkPermissions` → `validateResponse` → controller

- Mutating routes: always `checkPermissions`
- Controllers: no perm checks; pass `req.user` only when service needs scope/self ACL

## Layer ownership

- **route:** wire path, Zod, perms, upload — no business logic
- **controller:** `req.validated` (+ user/files) → one service call → JSON — no mappers, no domain ifs
- **service:** rules, orchestration, `Response*`; call mappers; may decorate DTO after map
- **mapper:** pure DB ↔ DTO only (`_id`→`id`, Maps, money boundary)
- **repository:** DB only; optional `session?: DbSession`; no `Response*`
- **utils:** shared pure helpers — grep before adding

## Guards / transactions

- NEVER re-validate Zod shape in service
- Prefer one null-check after `updateById`/`removeById` for missing primary entity
- DO null-check related lookups you use (e.g. currency for `scale`)
- Multi-write → `withTransaction` + pass `session`; single-doc CRUD → no session
- External I/O (files, HTTP) outside the transaction

## Zod / tests

- API schemas: `packages/shared`. DB/server-only: `backend/src/schemas`. Import: `from '@remnant/shared'`
- Tests: `test/routes/<entity>.test.ts` + `test/factories/<entity>.factory.ts`; unit in `test/unit/`
